            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\": \"Spiritual adultery, idolatry, and covenant unfaithfulness to God, often representing apostasy or a corrupt religious and worldly system.\",\"primary_basis\": [\"Hosea 1:2\",\"Ezekiel 16:15-34\",\"Ezekiel 23:1-49\",\"Jeremiah 3:1-10\",\"Revelation 17:1-6\"],\"alternatives\": [{\"meaning\": \"A specific historical or future persecuting political empire, such as Pagan Rome, first-century Jerusalem, or a future antichrist global system.\",\"basis\": [\"Revelation 17:9-11\",\"Revelation 17:18\"],\"prominence\": \"common\"},{\"meaning\": \"The Papacy or the Roman Catholic Church, a view particularly prevalent in classical Protestant historicist interpretation.\",\"basis\": [\"Revelation 17:4-9\"],\"prominence\": \"common\"},{\"meaning\": \"Exploitative economic systems, materialism, and oppressive global commerce.\",\"basis\": [\"Isaiah 23:15-17\",\"Nahum 3:4\",\"Revelation 18:3\"],\"prominence\": \"minority\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\": true,\"confidence\": \"high\",\"notes\": \"The broad symbolism of a harlot representing covenant unfaithfulness and idolatry is an established consensus based heavily on the Old Testament prophets. However, identifying the specific historical referent of the Whore of Babylon in Revelation 17 remains highly debated among preterist, futurist, historicist, and idealist interpretative schools.\"}",
